    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>You teach broken truths how to be honest again.</em></p><p>Once per <strong>a Soma Break</strong>, when your faction would normally <strong>destroy</strong> or consume a <strong>Corrupted Spark step</strong> or similarly tainted occult element, you can instead perform a brief rite of penance and reframing (at least 10 minutes of focused narrative or ritual work).</p><ul><li>Instead of destroying it, you may <strong>purify</strong> or <strong>stabilize</strong> that Spark step into a usable, non-corrupt form, as defined by your Tikkun/Spark rules.</li><li>Reduce an appropriate <strong>Darkness Track</strong> by <strong>1</strong> (local, regional, or campaign-scale, at GM’s discretion).</li></ul><p>This does not make all corruption safe; it lets you salvage specific shards that were trying to be true all along.</p>",
